=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  - Data sources (web useTranslation only; controlled component): the parent props
    onExecute / onRequestDialog / onToggleFavorite / loading / lastStatus / isFavorite
    are bound through two P1/S8 seams — CommandDispatching (execute + requestConfirmation,
    reporting CommandExecutionEvent started/succeeded/failed/offline) and
    CommandFavoriteToggling — so CommandTileModel owns loading/lastStatus/isFavorite as
    derived state. No I/O in the view.
  - Composition (web clickable GlassPanel + ghost Star Button + AlertTriangle + Loader2/Icon):
      • Tile     -> Button(.plain) + TSMaterial.panel glass + variant-tone hover border
                    (web hoverStyles default→accent / danger / success); dims to 0.5 while
                    executing (web `loading && opacity-50`); whole tile activates (web onClick).
      • Star     -> sibling overlay Button (independent tap = web e.stopPropagation()),
                    star.fill+warning tone when favorite else star+muted (web amber-300 / muted),
                    aria = web t('commands.toggleFavorite','Toggle favorite'); .isSelected trait.
      • Danger   -> exclamationmark.triangle.fill, danger/0.6 (web AlertTriangle text-neon-red/50),
                    non-interactive; activation routes to requestConfirmation (web onRequestDialog).
      • Icon box -> ProgressView while executing else Image(systemName:) (web Loader2 / Icon),
                    neutral surface box (web bg surface-2 / text-muted).
      • Label    -> label (textPrimary) + optional sublabel (muted) + status line
                    (CommandTileOutcome → checkmark/exclamation glyph + tone, web ✓ green / red).
  - States (ALL rendered; each has a #if DEBUG preview + a model/adapter unit test):
      idle (resting icon+label, never blank) · executing (spinner + dimmed, web loading) ·
      succeeded (web ✓ green) · failed (web red) · stale (freshness chip, time-based —
      native live-state chrome, ADR-013) · offline (cached outcome kept + offline chip,
      activation blocked). Favorite on/off and dangerous are orthogonal modifiers.
  - i18n (P1/S10): web key preserved verbatim — "commands.toggleFavorite" = "Toggle favorite";
    per-command label/sublabel keys are dynamic (owned by the command catalog) and resolved
    through the same facade with the def's key+fallback (not redeclared). Native chrome keys
    namespaced commands.tile.* (hint.confirm/run, state.running/succeeded/failed,
    freshness.stale/offline). Referenced==declared verified: 8 referenced, 8 declared, 0 missing.
    NO English string literals in native code (all via CommandTileStrings + Text(verbatim:)).
  - Accessibility: tile carries label (command) + value (running/succeeded/failed/stale/offline)
    + hint (confirm vs run) + identifier (command-tile-<id>); favorite carries its own label +
    .isSelected + identifier (command-tile-favorite-<id>); danger badge accessibilityHidden;
    status/chip combine; Dynamic-Type system fonts; reduce-motion honored (hover animation +
    TSSkeleton-free spinner).
  - Telemetry (P1/S11): CommandTileModel.start() emits view.opened with surface slug
    "CommandTile" exactly once (asserted), OSLogCommandTileTelemetry default; prod injects
    the shared diagnostics adapter.

